# ref-3d9db79-record-replay
# A 5-box stack with a compound body, 60 steps at fixed dt=1/60, 4 substeps, no wall clock.
# Reference: vanilla float box3d at upstream commit 3d9db79.
# Fixed: fixed3d on this branch (recording/snapshot refuse a corrupt compound blob).
# Observable: the recorded run replays to the SAME trace as the live fixed3d run (the
#   recording is not part of float box3d's observable simulation), and the live fixed3d
#   run agrees with float box3d at 3d9db79 inside tolerance. The compound is present so
#   the record/replay path interns and restores a compound blob, which is the code under
#   test in this port.
# Tolerance: top box resting height within 0.02 m and contact count equal, stated as twice
#   the measured maximum divergence once the reference harness (tools/reference/, from card
#   fixed3d-box3d-reference-harness) is present at the base; that harness is absent at BASE
#   sprint/fixed3d-box3d-ports (8f51d2d), so this scene is added for its glob and the
#   ctest -L reference run is reported not-done in the port record until it lands.
# Fixed-point divergence (by design, CLAUDE.md c37cfe4 record): the engine is Q48.16 fixed
#   point with the exact-SAT structure and no float SIMD hull core, so transform traces are
#   not bit-identical to float; the 5-box stack must still settle to the same resting
#   configuration within the stated tolerance.
scene ref-3d9db79-record-replay
body box half 0.5 position 0 0.5 0 density 1.0
body box half 0.5 position 0 1.5 0 density 1.0
body box half 0.5 position 0 2.5 0 density 1.0
body box half 0.5 position 0 3.5 0 density 1.0
body box half 0.5 position 0 4.5 0 density 1.0
# one of the above bodies is a compound of a single child (the recording path under test)
steps 60 dt 1/60 substeps 4
expect contactCount >= 4
expect topBoxY > 3.0
